{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::graph` MUST expose the graph's associated types and content lookup operation:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Graph: Send + Sync {\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: Send + Sync;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n    type Error: Send;\n\n    // Outgoing edges and judgment metadata are specified separately.\n    fn node_content(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n}\n```\n\nThe SDK MUST leave the domain meaning of node identities, edges, and contents\nto the consumer.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations**\n1. `habeas_sdk::graph` exposes a `Graph` trait. Its associated types are `NodeId`, `NodeContent`, `EdgeLabel` and `Error`, with the stated bounds.\n2. `Graph` has a `node_content(&self, &NodeId) -> Result<NodeContent, Error>` lookup.\n3. The SDK leaves the domain meaning of node ids, edges and contents to the consumer.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- **Trait and types are consumed by many separate implementations.** Each implements the trait and fills every associated type with a different domain type:\n  - `tests/agent.rs` `impl[Memory/Graph]` uses `Node`, `Contents`, `Label` and `io::Error`.\n  - The `tests/contracts.rs` `macro[graph]` uses `Node`, `Content`, `u8` and `&'static str`.\n  - `tests/validation.rs` `impl[Memory/Graph]` uses `u8`, `String`, `u8` and `&'static str`.\n  - `tests/storage.rs` `impl[StoredGraph/Graph]` uses `String`, `()`, `()` and `FileStorageError`.\n  - `src/sdk.rs` `impl[HabeasDomain/Graph]` uses `HabeasNode`, `ResolvedInput`, `HabeasEdgeLabel` and `io::Error`.\n\n  The associated-type obligations and the \"SDK leaves meaning to the consumer\" obligation are compile-time properties. These implementations compile against the trait, which exercises both.\n- **Bounds.** The `Send`, `Sync`, `Clone` and `Eq` bounds are checked at compile time. The `send(...)` helper in `checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata` additionally requires the futures built over the graph to be `Send`.\n- **Content lookup success.**\n  - `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` and `validation_is_usable_without_any_evidence_storage` both assert the returned content. The first checks that the dependency fingerprint equals \"source\". The second checks that it equals \"ordinary computation\". The first also checks that the chat history contains the content.\n  - `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` calls `node_content` on a `HabeasDomain` and asserts the resulting input JSON and fingerprints. It does this both before and after the source file changes.\n- **Content lookup failure.** `checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata` makes the read fail and asserts that the consumer's `Error` value (`\"read\"`) is returned. This covers the `Result<_, Self::Error>` signature.\n\n**Gaps**\nNone found. The tests are adequate for this requirement. Outgoing edges and judgment metadata are explicitly specified elsewhere.",
  "references": "4578c86bf218e8b292db3680c8f24d73bcb4085daebf10e9442c0b7a0144427c",
  "inputs": [
